katana-icons

The kanji codes (packages/static/svg/kanji, packages/react/src/kanji.js, line/kanji.json) are
outlines of glyphs from Dela Gothic One, Copyright 2020 The Dela Gothic Project Authors,
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (https://openfontlicense.org). Source:
https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/delagothicone (read 2026-11-26).

The squircle corners in line/set/katana.mjs follow the algorithm of figma-squircle
(https://github.com/phamfoo/figma-squircle, MIT, read 2026-11-26).

KT Stencil (type/dist/*.ttf, *.woff2) and the stencil icons (packages/static/svg/stencil) are drawn
by KATANA, following the publicly described approach of mecha-cockpit screen type (straight
strokes, stencil bridges, readability first). No glyphs were copied from any existing font.
The fonts are released under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

packages/fonts/ also redistributes, as WOFF2 subsets, these fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(sources: https://github.com/google/fonts, read 2026-11-26; licence texts in packages/fonts/licenses/):
Michroma (The Michroma Project Authors), Dela Gothic One (The Dela Gothic Project Authors),
Shippori Mincho and Shippori Mincho B1 (The Shippori Mincho Project Authors), Zen Kaku Gothic New (The Zen Kaku Gothic Project Authors),
Archivo (The Archivo Project Authors), DotGothic16 (The DotGothic16 Project Authors), Doto (The Doto Project Authors),
Noto Sans SC (Adobe, Reserved Font Name 'Source'), Barlow Condensed (The Barlow Project Authors), DM Mono (The DM Mono Project Authors),
Maple Mono NF CN (The Maple Mono Project Authors; Latin subset taken from KatanaUI), Ark Pixel Font (TakWolf; CJK subset taken from KatanaUI),
Silkscreen (The Silkscreen Project Authors), Pixelify Sans (The Pixelify Sans Project Authors), VT323 (The VT323 Project Authors).
KT Stencil, KT Stencil Solid, KT Pixel and KT Dot (type/dist/): Latin glyphs and a few kanji are drawn by KATANA;
the other CJK glyphs are straightened from the stroke medians of Make Me a Hanzi (graphics.txt,
https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi, read 2026-11-26), which is derived from Arphic PL KaitiM GB and
Arphic PL UKai and licensed under the Arphic Public License. The four fonts are therefore distributed under the
Arphic Public License (text in type/APL.txt and packages/fonts/licenses/APL-kt-fonts.txt).
Subsetting changes no glyph; the Reserved Font Names are kept.
